    <div class="panel">
      <div class="controls">
        <div class="ctl"><span>Measure</span>${segHTML('gapM',[['total','Total'],['carry','Carry']],gapMetric)}</div>
        <div class="ctl"><span>Window</span>${segHTML('gapW',[['14','2 weeks'],['30','30 days'],['all','All time']],gapWindow)}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="plot">${g.svg}</div>
      <p class="caption">Notch = median, bracket = P25–P75. Overlap measured as P90 of the shorter club against P10
      of the longer: ${g.laps.length?g.laps.join(' · '):'none worth calling out'}. Where two ridges share a window,
      the two clubs are doing the same job on their good and bad days.
      ${g.windowed?`Trailing ${gapWindow==='14'?'2 weeks':'30 days'} only (${g.n.toLocaleString()} shots) — a swing or club
      change won't get diluted by everything hit before it.`:`Showing all-time data${gapWindow!=='all'?" — nothing hit in that window recently, so this is every shot on record instead":''}.`}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="blockhead">
      <h2>By club</h2>
      <span class="sub">Latest session median, versus the three before it. Grey means the move is inside noise.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="cards">${CLUB_LIST.slice().sort(byLoft).map(club=>{
      const sess=sessionsOf(club,3), n=clubRows(club).length;
